@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk User Integration
	Testing user sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View new users
	New users who are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View resynced users
	Users who are resynced to Zendesk via OSB should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given I remove a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove a user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I sync the project with the code "ZENOSBA" to zendesk
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View resynced deleted users
	Deleted users who are resynced to Zendesk via OSB should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I sync the project with the code "ZENOSBA" to zendesk
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View customer role updates
	Existing users who are changed from Developer to Watcher and vice versa on OSB should have their respective Zendesk tags updated.

	Given I update a customer on the project with the code "ZENOSBA" with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the role of "Watcher"
	And I update a customer on the project with the code "ZENOSBA" with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the role of "Developer"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag

Scenario: View expired project user updates
	If a project's order becomes inactive in OSB, existing users on that project should have their tags removed and also be removed from their organization in Zendesk.

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"

Scenario: View customer removal updates
	If a customer is removed from a project in OSB, the customer's tags should be removed and the customer should also be removed from the organization in Zendesk.

	Given I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"

Scenario: View watcher removal updates
	If a watcher is removed from a project in OSB, the watcher's tags should be removed and the watcher should also be removed from the organization in Zendesk.

	Given I remove a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"

Scenario: View no support ticket project user updates
	If a project's order becomes inactive in OSB, existing users on that project should have their tags removed and also be removed from their organization in Zendesk.

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to not have support tickets for the product "Portal Production"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"

Scenario: View no support ticket project to expired project user updates
	If a project's order becomes inactive in OSB, existing users on that project should have their tags removed and also be removed from their organization in Zendesk.

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to not have support tickets for the product "Portal Production"
	And I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"